'''Ancient Forest Labyrinth''' (古代樹の迷宮 ''Kodaiju no Meikyū'', "'''Labyrinth of Ancient Trees'''" or "'''Labyrinth of the Ancient Tree'''") is the 36th sub-chapter of [[Uncanny Legends]], and the 85th sub-chapter overall. It was added in [[Version 10.6 Update|Version 10.6]], and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty. The [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] is in every stage except the last.

After clearing [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Eldritch Forces Invasion]] and all 1-Crown Uncanny Legends sub-chapters, the final stage in the 1-Crown version of this sub-chapter will be [[The Face of God/Invasion|invaded]] by [[Idi:Ne]]. Upon being cleared, the stage returns to its normal state.

==Difficulty==
All of the stages abuse [[Surge Attack|Surge]] gimmicks to an unprecedented degree, requiring players to find ways around them. Although the enemy compositions aren't too challenging themselves, [[Re-Leaf Towers]] may catch players by surprise on first try.

The [[The Face of God/Invasion|Invasion]] stage's difficulty remains to be determined.
{{LegendDiff|130|170|100}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces 2 new enemies:
*[[Elder Flame Doron]]: A long-ranged kamikaze [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy that is extremely durable. He attacks only once, but deals heavy damage, creates a Lv.8 [[Surge Attack]], and weakens cats to 1% for 40 seconds.
*[[Idi:Ne]]: A rusher-type Relic appearing in the [[The Face of God/Invasion|The Face of God Invasion]]. Behaves just like [[Idi:Re]], but has weaker overall stats and is immune to [[Wave Attack|Waves]] and Surges.

The Face of God Invasion is also the first non-event stage with a [[Base Barrier]], a mechanic originally introduced in [[Anniversary/11 1/2 Year#Disaster in the Wan Wan Kingdom|Disaster in the Wan Wan Kingdom]]. The Base Barrier renders the stage's enemy base invulnerable until the boss is defeated, after which the Base Barrier is permanently shattered. Since it's distinct from [[Barrier]]s and [[Shield]]s, it takes no effect from [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]], the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] and [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing]].

When the normal version of the final stage is completed, players have a 30% chance to unlock Elder Flame Doron as a [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Unit]] (guaranteed if a [[Treasure Radar]] is used). The invaded version is guaranteed to drop [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]]'s [[True Form]] upon being cleared.

